## Installation

$ rpm -Uvh --noplugins /tmp/gdbm-1.8.3-1.9.armv7l.rpm /tmp/libllvm-22.1.8-2.1.armv7l.rpm /tmp/perl-5.42.0-1.9.armv7l.rpm /tmp/linux-kernel-perf-6.12.80-0.armv7l.rpm
Preparing... [100%]
Updating / installing...
1:libllvm-22.1.8-2.1 [25%]
2:gdbm-1.8.3-1.9 [50%]
/sbin/ldconfig: Cannot lstat /lib/libgdbm.so.3.0.0: Permission denied
/sbin/ldconfig: Cannot lstat /lib/libLLVM.so.22.1: Permission denied
3:perl-5.42.0-1.9 [75%]
4:linux-kernel-perf-6.12.80-0 [100%]

The transaction completed without a dependency refusal, so no dependency
retry was used. Subsequent `ldd /usr/bin/perf` resolved every NEEDED library,
`rpm -V` returned no differences with rc=0, and perf executed successfully.

installed=linux-kernel-perf-6.12.80-0.armv7l
installed=libllvm-22.1.8-2.1.armv7l
